// Variant: Alternating Clues & Brown (5 Suits). 3 players, our_player_index=1.

// Forced-endgame Rule 5 — "the partner needs two turns".
//
// `Alternating Clues & Brown (5 Suits)`, stacks [5,4,4,5,4] = 22/25 with ONE
// card left and 2 clues. Alice is will-bot67; will-bot69 holds BOTH the g5 and
// the y5, each playable and each the last copy.
//
//   Alice draws the last card -> final round is will-bot69, yagami_black,
//     Alice. will-bot69 gets ONE turn, cashes one 5, and the other dies. 24/25.
//   Alice stalls              -> will-bot69 plays and draws, so the final round
//     is yagami_black, Alice, will-bot69. He cashes both. 25/25.
//
// The bot discarded order 46. `forced_endgame_action` was entered and DECLINED
// -- Rule 4 wants `cards_left == 2` and criticals in Alice's OWN hand -- so
// `decide.cpp` fell through to `endgame.honours_reacter_call` and spent the turn
// on a standing urgent CTD. The priority was never inverted; the rule was
// missing.
//
// v11.0.0 fixes this TWICE OVER, which is why the assertion is on the action
// rather than on which layer produced it. Rule 5 forces the stall directly; and
// independently, target parity now stands down at 60% (22/25 is past it), so the
// rank-3 clue to Bob on turn 51 reads STABLE and never creates the urgent CTD
// that took the turn. Verified separately: either change alone yields the stall.
